{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a Cp*Co(III)-catalyzed synthesis of multi-substituted isoquinolines via site-selective C-H activation of unsymmetrical O-acyloximes. The cobalt catalyst demonstrates superior site selectivity (favoring the less sterically hindered C-H bond) and higher reactivity toward terminal alkynes compared to traditional Cp*Rh(III) catalysts. The reaction utilizes the N-O bond of the oxime as an internal oxidant, making the process redox-neutral.",
